1
00:00:11,458 --> 00:00:12,833
Our camp is just up ahead.

2
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:15,208
Take a right at that
intersection and we're there.

3
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Slow down, slow down.

4
00:00:32,208 --> 00:00:33,208
It's right up ahead.

5
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,333
This is my place.

6
00:00:50,041 --> 00:00:51,041
Mom!

7
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:52,375
Chengren!

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,333
Your leg!

9
00:00:53,416 --> 00:00:55,666
How did this happen?

10
00:00:55,875 --> 00:00:57,040
It hurts so bad.

11
00:00:57,041 --> 00:00:58,874
Quick, get inside.

12
00:00:58,875 --> 00:00:59,875
Hurry!

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
"The Last Oath"

14
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,000
(Episode 7: Class A Infected)

15
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,916
Ever since your dad died,

16
00:02:20,458 --> 00:02:22,000
it's just been the two of us.

17
00:02:25,416 --> 00:02:27,541
If anything were to happen to you,

18
00:02:29,083 --> 00:02:30,958
what would I do?

19
00:02:34,083 --> 00:02:35,541
We have no food,

20
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:36,916
and no medicine.

21
00:02:37,833 --> 00:02:38,916
We can't stay in this dump

22
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:42,041
for much longer.

23
00:02:43,708 --> 00:02:44,708
And now you're hurt.

24
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:45,708
Mom,

25
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:46,791
please stop crying.

26
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,500
It's all my fault.

27
00:02:48,958 --> 00:02:49,958
It's my fault for being useless.

28
00:02:49,959 --> 00:02:50,999
I couldn't catch any game,

29
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,000
and I even got myself hurt.

30
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:54,250
I'm just a burden to you.

31
00:02:58,875 --> 00:02:59,458
Ma'am.

32
00:02:59,791 --> 00:03:00,791
Please don't cry.

33
00:03:02,416 --> 00:03:03,666
We injured him by accident.

34
00:03:03,916 --> 00:03:05,156
We'll take full responsibility.

35
00:03:09,791 --> 00:03:10,911
We'll stay here for a while.

36
00:03:18,125 --> 00:03:19,125
The situation here...

37
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:20,625
you've seen it yourselves.

38
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:23,250
If you just leave us be,

39
00:03:24,416 --> 00:03:26,000
a widow and her son,

40
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:28,666
we really won't survive.

41
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:32,333
Don't worry.

42
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,140
We'll go out and find some food tomorrow.

43
00:03:40,916 --> 00:03:41,916
It's too late today.

44
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:44,101
We have some crackers in our bag.

45
00:03:44,125 --> 00:03:45,205
Have some to hold you over.

46
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:54,541
How long have you lived here?

47
00:03:57,291 --> 00:03:58,451
Are there any zombies nearby?

48
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:02,583
It's been a while.

49
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:04,916
Ever since we got here,

50
00:04:05,375 --> 00:04:06,750
we haven't seen a single zombie.

51
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:09,125
It's very safe here.

52
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Come with me.

53
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:27,916
We don't have much space.

54
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:33,916
We can make a bed for one of you here.

55
00:04:34,916 --> 00:04:36,083
But it needs some tidying up.

56
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:38,041
There's a small shed outside.

57
00:04:38,375 --> 00:04:39,416
The other can sleep there.

58
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,500
Right here.

59
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:44,958
Then he can...

60
00:04:45,041 --> 00:04:46,041
He'll sleep with me.

61
00:04:54,083 --> 00:04:54,875
It's fine, ma'am.

62
00:04:55,083 --> 00:04:55,750
This will do.

63
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:56,791
Get some rest.

64
00:04:56,791 --> 00:04:57,791
Don't worry about us.

65
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:15,788
It shouldn't take too long.

66
00:05:16,125 --> 00:05:17,925
I feel like we can leave
in a couple of days.

67
00:05:19,791 --> 00:05:20,791
No rush.

68
00:05:22,291 --> 00:05:23,891
You're actually not in a hurry to leave?

69
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:26,458
You saw the boat, right?

70
00:05:27,166 --> 00:05:28,458
We'll check on it tomorrow.

71
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:30,348
Once it's fixed, we'll take the waterway.

72
00:05:47,916 --> 00:05:48,916
You're not sleeping yet?

73
00:05:49,708 --> 00:05:50,708
You go ahead.

74
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,041
Heading out?

75
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:51,625
Don't worry, ma'am.

76
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,041
We'll be back with food.

77
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,040
The hull is mostly intact.

78
00:07:49,666 --> 00:07:50,666
The gas tank is empty.

79
00:08:01,083 --> 00:08:02,083
And the wiring is shot.

80
00:08:03,791 --> 00:08:05,541
If we can find some wires and diesel,

81
00:08:06,791 --> 00:08:07,911
we should be able to fix it.

82
00:08:08,708 --> 00:08:09,708
Then let's get looking.

83
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,250
Still hungry?

84
00:08:28,291 --> 00:08:29,041
I'm not stupid.

85
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:30,490
Last time was a total accident.

86
00:08:32,083 --> 00:08:33,283
If you don't look for trouble,

87
00:08:33,375 --> 00:08:34,535
there won't be any accidents.

88
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:42,333
Mount Zhiliao.

89
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:45,583
This waterway leads back to our old camp.

90
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:47,830
How are things on your end?

91
00:09:49,166 --> 00:09:50,958
I found some usable wires.

92
00:09:52,666 --> 00:09:53,208
Then we're all set.

93
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:54,375
Let's go.

94
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:49,458
You're back.

95
00:10:49,541 --> 00:10:51,101
It must have been a long day out there.

96
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:52,333
I just made some soup.

97
00:10:52,833 --> 00:10:54,393
With some wild greens I picked outside.

98
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:55,166
Have a sip.

99
00:10:55,291 --> 00:10:56,291
Quench your thirst.

100
00:10:59,583 --> 00:11:00,583
I'm not thirsty.

101
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:04,166
Neither of us is thirsty.

102
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:06,166
Ma'am,

103
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:07,666
you guys have it.

104
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:10,708
My mom spent ages cooking this.

105
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:11,750
If you won't drink it,

106
00:11:12,875 --> 00:11:13,875
then I will.

107
00:11:20,875 --> 00:11:22,355
We brought back quite a bit of stuff.

108
00:11:29,625 --> 00:11:31,165
You guys are amazing.

109
00:11:31,166 --> 00:11:32,375
So much good food!

110
00:11:33,291 --> 00:11:34,531
Let's split it down the middle.

111
00:11:40,541 --> 00:11:41,875
My son's leg...

112
00:11:42,083 --> 00:11:43,374
I don't know when

113
00:11:43,375 --> 00:11:44,916
it'll fully heal.

114
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,249
He can't work,

115
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:48,791
and he's just a burden.

116
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:51,291
And an old woman like me

117
00:11:51,916 --> 00:11:53,500
is useless too.

118
00:11:54,541 --> 00:11:55,625
To make some soup,

119
00:11:55,791 --> 00:11:57,083
I could only find some

120
00:11:57,166 --> 00:11:58,833
wild greens.

121
00:12:05,541 --> 00:12:06,541
Just take it for now.

122
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:09,283
We can always find more later.

123
00:12:11,041 --> 00:12:12,041
Thank you.

124
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,583
Thank you, young man.

125
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:15,041
You're both good people.

126
00:12:15,541 --> 00:12:17,000
Eat up, eat up.

127
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:19,666
Hurry and eat.

128
00:12:43,333 --> 00:12:44,333
What's the problem?

129
00:12:46,625 --> 00:12:47,625
The fuel line is clogged.

130
00:12:48,083 --> 00:12:49,083
Is it an easy fix?

131
00:12:49,708 --> 00:12:50,708
It's not hard.

132
00:12:51,166 --> 00:12:52,166
Just time-consuming.

133
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:56,583
Come on, let's head to the east woods.

134
00:12:57,916 --> 00:12:59,356
I still need to clear the fuel line.

135
00:13:00,583 --> 00:13:01,791
I plan on leaving tomorrow.

136
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:03,453
We need to stock up on food.

137
00:13:06,083 --> 00:13:07,083
Tomorrow?

138
00:13:07,583 --> 00:13:09,125
Then we should fix the boat ASAP.

139
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,041
Tell you what,

140
00:13:13,541 --> 00:13:15,021
you go hunt, and I'll keep fixing it.

141
00:13:15,708 --> 00:13:16,708
No way.

142
00:13:17,083 --> 00:13:18,083
We go together.

143
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:20,750
Why?

144
00:13:20,958 --> 00:13:22,226
You can hunt just fine on your own.

145
00:13:22,250 --> 00:13:23,850
And you can't help with the boat anyway.

146
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:25,250
You want to leave as soon as possible,

147
00:13:25,251 --> 00:13:26,476
but you refuse to split up the work.

148
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,291
What exactly do you want?

149
00:13:27,292 --> 00:13:28,500
I can't leave you alone.

150
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,500
It's dangerous here.

151
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:43,041
Dangerous?

152
00:13:43,958 --> 00:13:44,958
A-Leh,

153
00:13:45,208 --> 00:13:46,000
just because I'm going with you

154
00:13:46,166 --> 00:13:47,458
doesn't mean I'm your prisoner.

155
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:49,083
Me fixing the boat here

156
00:13:49,084 --> 00:13:50,208
is just to help you out.

157
00:14:02,666 --> 00:14:03,666
We don't have much time.

158
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:06,256
Let's not waste it keeping
tabs on each other.

159
00:14:36,291 --> 00:14:37,291
You're back.

160
00:14:37,625 --> 00:14:38,791
That's a really fat chicken.

161
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:42,875
Look, a chicken!

162
00:14:57,875 --> 00:14:58,875
You're heading out again?

163
00:15:04,458 --> 00:15:05,458
What took you so long?

164
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:07,708
What?

165
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:08,833
Afraid I'd run off?

166
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:11,750
Ma'am,

167
00:15:11,916 --> 00:15:12,934
we're having chicken tonight...!

168
00:15:12,958 --> 00:15:14,124
Your friend is really something.

169
00:15:14,125 --> 00:15:15,541
It's been ages since we had meat.

170
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:27,390
Your hands are dirty. Go wash them first.
